Test & Build	Build Docker image	2026-10-12T09:03:36.3992197Z             "body": "Refs #200.\r\n\r\nInstrument CSV/TXT/XLSX files can be mapped to the current run's instrument, previewed, then imported atomically. Unknown sample IDs remain visible and skipped; a conflict on a matched row refuses the entire file with zero writes. Successful imports create raw drafts and pending QC observations through their existing owners, plus an immutable source receipt. Recording, calculation, QC evaluation and workflow decisions remain explicit actions.\r\n\r\nThe workbench provides scoped mappings and immutable revisions, current activated calculation inputs, per-cell issues, preview invalidation and all five languages. Paste matches lab labels and supports comma, semicolon and tab delimiters. XLSX retains decoded source evidence and uses the approved separator-only round trip through the unchanged lab-number parser. No unit conversion, dilution calculation, formula execution or scientific defaults are inferred.\r\n\r\nThis existing PR is merged with released main 51f6798806f630773786a08432290c1b21a841da at draft head 36ee761789a1eb42bceee537ff419456f6cd484d. It retains PR293's selected reported-value exports and #283's analysis-unit authority. The 17 application conflicts are resolved.\r\n\r\nIntegration scope requiring exact-head review:\r\n- The additive installer creates only two immutable tables/guards, nullable restrictive WorkItemDraft.importReceiptId, and one installation receipt. Native ALTER retains existing drafts; no rebuild, adoption or analytical backfill.\r\n- A new digest-bound, finite predecessor-DDL oracle explicitly protects #205 WorkItemDraft.records in the current fresh and native-ALTER variants. Unknown columns or changed types refuse. The old 89/92-model literals and closed factories remain unchanged; an additional closed schema-only fixture contains the unmodified Prisma emission from main51f.\r\n- Installer row preservation now streams exactly the original JSON hash/order using original columns, including records. The populated predecessor test compares it with the original array hash and verifies every retained row, schema, FK, backup hash and zero-change repeat.\r\n- Local tests may select one explicitly named metadata-only template under tests/.owned-templates. The closed selector rejects working/production/aliased paths. Normal global setup, owned suite copies, teardown and published Help checks remain. Original DB/WAL/SHM files remain byte-identical.\r\n\r\nDependency authorization is already recorded: YY's \"approve saxes, clear the hold\" on PR284 comments 6099365745/6099368373 covers saxes 6.0.0 (ISC) and locked xmlchars 2.2.0 (MIT). ZIP decoding uses built-in Node zlib; the client XLSX library is not used for these uploads. Caps are 16 MiB upload, 64 MiB uncompressed, 4096 ZIP entries, 250000 XML nodes, depth 64 and 4096 merge ranges. Unsupported/encrypted/macro/external/formula/date/error/ambiguous-number inputs refuse without writes; no extraction, external loading or entity expansion.\r\n\r\nValidation at this integrated draft is IN PROGRESS, not audit-ready:\r\n- Six focused suites: 128/128 pass, including retained reported-value exports, analysis-unit authority, installer preservation and SQL scanner.\r\n- Import/startup group: 451 pass and one missing paste-locale block failure retained. Both new locale blocks are now present in all five languages with every prior main value unchanged; corrected paste/UI group passes 27/27.\r\n- Client build passes; lint has 0 errors and 14 existing warnings.\r\n- Original integrated full local run failed 6 tests (355/360 suites), and CI38215041808 failed the two unresolved test SQL calls (359/360 suites); raw logs retained. SQL is now explicit and inspectable, with scanner rules unchanged. Rooted SPA/download delivery also fixes hidden workspace parent paths; request dotfiles remain blocked. The six affected suites pass 213/213.\r\n- Fresh normal unfiltered 360-suite local run and exact-head CI38218977639, including both actual Docker acceptance gates, are running at the new head. No full-green claim yet.\r\n\r\nRaw provenance, earlier failures and current validation evidence are retained on audit/release-eb6de2e8 in WP/pr284-resume-20261012. Source guard precedent 6089928620 and all #200 pins apply, including latest numeric pin6096643904. See docs/audit/200-instrument-import.md. No #200 production installer or deployment has run; it will require a new reviewed source/proof/frozen kit and fresh single-use gate under YY's standing go. Claudio owns the post-deploy check and issue closure.\r\n",
